      "message": "What happens is that:\n1. C Binder is built-in to core kernel.\n2. Rust Binder is a module.\n\nDuring loading Rust Binder we decide whether to use Rust or C Binder. If we use C Binder, then Rust Binder calls `binder_remove_trace_events()` with a pointer to the Rust Binder module. If we use Rust Binder, then C Binder calls `binder_remove_trace_events()` with a null pointer.",
